@page "/demos/controlled-components"
@using Dottor.BlazorConf2026.Components.Demos.Demo02

<PageTitle>Demo 2 - Controlled Components</PageTitle>

<div class="mb-4">
    <h2>🎛️ Demo 2: Controlled Components</h2>
    <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
        <strong>Pattern:</strong> A controlled component does <em>not</em> own its state.
        It receives a <code>Value</code>, renders it, and notifies changes via <code>ValueChanged</code>.
        The parent is the single source of truth.
    </div>
    <div class="alert alert-light border mb-0 py-2">
        <strong>🎤 Live demo:</strong> Select some stars on the <span class="text-danger fw-bold">left</span>, then click
        <em>"Reset from Parent → 1"</em>. The stars <strong>won't reset</strong> because the child keeps its own copy.
        Now try the same on the <span class="text-success fw-bold">right</span> — it works perfectly because there's a single source of truth.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row g-4">
    @* ─── PROBLEM ─── *@
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card border-danger h-100">
            <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                <span>❌ Problem: Uncontrolled (Duplicated State)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p class="text-muted small">
                    The child copies the initial value in <code>OnInitialized</code> and manages its own <code>_internalValue</code>.
                    After the parent resets its value, the child still shows the old one.
                </p>

                <div class="mb-3">
                    <UncontrolledRating @bind-Value="_brokenRating" />
                </div>

                <div class="d-flex gap-2 mb-3">
                    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" @onclick="() => _brokenRating = 1">
                        Reset from Parent → 1
                    </button>
                    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" @onclick="() => _brokenRating = 5">
                        Set from Parent → 5
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="card bg-light border">
                    <div class="card-body py-2 small font-monospace">
                        <div>Parent value: <span class="badge bg-primary">@_brokenRating</span></div>
                        <div>Child renders: <span class="badge bg-danger bg-opacity-75">its own _internalValue</span></div>
                        <div class="mt-1 text-danger fw-bold">
                            @if (_brokenRating != _brokenLastClicked && _brokenLastClicked > 0)
                            {
                                <span>⚠️ State mismatch! Parent says @_brokenRating, child may show something else</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>Click Reset to see the mismatch</span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ─── SOLUTION ─── *@
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card border-success h-100">
            <div class="card-header bg-success text-white d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                <span>✅ Solution: Controlled (Single Source of Truth)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p class="text-muted small">
                    The child has <strong>zero internal state</strong>. It renders <code>Value</code> from the parent
                    and notifies via <code>ValueChanged</code>. Supports <code>@@bind-Value</code> out of the box.
                </p>

                <div class="mb-3">
                    <div class="d-flex gap-1 align-items-center">
                        <ControlledRating @bind-Value="_fixedRating" />
                        <span class="badge bg-success bg-opacity-75 ms-2">
                            value: @_fixedRating
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="d-flex gap-2 mb-3">
                    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" @onclick="() => _fixedRating = 1">
                        Reset from Parent → 1
                    </button>
                    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" @onclick="() => _fixedRating = 5">
                        Set from Parent → 5
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="card bg-light border">
                    <div class="card-body py-2 small font-monospace">
                        <div>Parent value: <span class="badge bg-primary">@_fixedRating</span></div>
                        <div>Child renders: <span class="badge bg-success bg-opacity-75">same Value from parent</span></div>
                        <div class="mt-1 text-success fw-bold">✅ Always in sync</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-light border rounded">
    <h6>🔑 Key Points</h6>
    <ul class="mb-0">
        <li>The <strong>uncontrolled</strong> version stores <code>_internalValue</code> in <code>OnInitialized</code> — it drifts from the parent.</li>
        <li>The <strong>controlled</strong> version has zero internal state: <code>Value</code> in, <code>ValueChanged</code> out.</li>
        <li>Supports <code>@@bind-Value</code> out of the box (convention: <code>Value</code> + <code>ValueChanged</code>).</li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    private int _brokenRating = 3;
    private int _brokenLastClicked;
    private int _fixedRating = 3;
}
